{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>A rod of לבנה.</b> It is a tree, and its name is לבנה, as you would say ״תַּחַת אַלּוֹן וְלִבְנֶה״ (Hosea 4). And I say it is what they call טרינבל\"א בְּלַעַ\"ז, which is white." "<b>לח.</b> When it is moist." "<b>לוז.</b> And he also took a rod of לוז — a tree on which thin nuts grow; קולדו\"י בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>And plane tree.</b> קשטני\"יר בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Peeled strips.</b> Peelings, peelings — he would make it speckled." "<b>The peeled white.</b> The exposed white of the rod — when he would peel it, its white would appear and be revealed in the peeled place."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French tremble, 'poplar' (the aspen, white-barked)", 2 "the la'az is Old French coudre/noisetier, 'hazelnut'", 3 "the la'az is Old French châtaignier, 'chestnut tree'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:24.190130037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}